  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186083201,
      "id": "dc6d9b69-0459-515a-ba7b-c62cab96ca00",
      "title": "Identifying Divergent Improper Integrals"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ac345da4-8918-5f2e-a45c-24f932e8b9ff",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{27}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we substitute $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\frac{1}{x}\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $u\\to \\infty $ when $x\\to \\infty ,$ the table for the limits of integration using the rule $u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 27 & \\infty  \\\\ u & \\operatorname{ln}⁡27 & \\infty \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable $u$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{27}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡27}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{27}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡27}^{a}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡u]}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡27}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }[\\operatorname{ln}⁡a-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡27)] \\\\  & =\\infty -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡27) \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a1b11563-9fad-5885-aaee-c7e34e34b008",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "469caa51-3e0e-5203-9e87-66b4d0ae571f",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\operatorname{ln}{\\left(27 \\right)}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6c1b8667-8e70-5dc5-84d7-174a917db534",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "The integral is divergent"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "83e23ebc-479b-5f99-9d7f-da779d1784b0",
