    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e8916bb6-53e9-5fde-91ee-b82ad183c20c",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}z}{z}.$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}z}{z} & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}\\frac{\\text{d}z}{z} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡z]}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & ={lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{ln}⁡a-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =\\infty -\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =\\infty .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the integral is divergent.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "c03102d6-d1cf-576a-a5f3-a3a99cd0d5f0",
